Unreleased
==========

Symbolic trie
-------------

- Added an in-memory symbolic-trie index with configurable 2-, 4-, or 8-way
  fanout, leaf capacity, sampled root splitting, and entropy × variance-based
  splits.
- Separates the trie word into independently configurable concerns: node and
  leaf MBRs may use up to 128 transform dimensions (capped by series length),
  split selection uses a configurable prefix, and record bounds use a
  configurable 16--64-dimension symbolic prefix.
- Supports SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words, including integer input files,
  optional z-normalization, and query-specific symbolic lower-bound tables.
- Uses node-MBR pruning plus best-first leaf scans, ordered by record lower
  bounds, with exact-distance early abandonment.  The disjoint leaf-MBR
  suffix contribution is enabled by default and combines dimensions outside
  the record prefix with its symbolic bound; it can be disabled with
  `--no-trie-record-mbr-suffix-bound`.
- Added an optional post-build, flat k-means directory inside large SFA, PISA,
  and SPARTAN trie leaves (`--trie-leaf-ivf K`).  Cluster MBR bounds prune
  groups before their records are scanned, without changing the main trie or
  using raw-space centroid/radius bounds; eligible leaves are clustered in
  parallel during construction.
- Added float32 SIMD per-record radial pruning for trie IVF leaves, including
  `--trie-leaf-ivf-radial-bound-auto`, which keeps the bound only when a
  query-local 64 K candidate sample rejects at least 25%.
- Removes the redundant full root-MBR scan after a successful root split by
  merging the child MBRs already formed during partitioning.
- Provides batch and single-query parallel modes with configurable worker and
  queue counts, plus construction, coverage, and per-phase query timings.
- Reports split occupancy, non-empty-child, and largest-child diagnostics to
  make fanout experiments directly comparable.  Query summaries now separate
  node-MBR, leaf-cluster-MBR, and record-prefix/suffix pruning stages.

SIMD and distance kernels
-------------------------

- Improved BSF-aware SIMD Euclidean-distance and symbolic lower-bound paths,
  including register-only horizontal reductions and alignment selection
  outside the vector loop where supported.
- Added scalar-reference coverage for exact distance and lower-bound SIMD
  kernels, plus a target-CPU exact-distance microbenchmark.
- Configuration output now identifies the SIMD instruction set in use (or
  states when no SIMD ISA was compiled in).
- Record lower-bound lookup tables support all configured trie record-prefix
  widths (16--64 dimensions) in both SIMD and scalar paths.

Transforms and PCA projection
-----------------------------

- PISA uses the independent coordinates of the full real FFT before PCA, with
  the appropriate real-spectrum weighting and mean-coefficient handling.
- SPARTAN and PISA bulk trie construction project records in blocks through
  optional CBLAS SGEMM.  Builds retain a scalar fallback when CBLAS is absent;
  a single-threaded OpenBLAS installation splits an SGEMM block across OpenMP
  workers, while threaded OpenBLAS keeps ownership of parallelism.
- Build and run output state which PCA projection path is active, including
  the detected OpenBLAS configuration when available.

Sampling
--------

- Reworked SPARTAN uniform and random binning samples to read contiguous
  blocks instead of seeking separately for every sampled record.  This avoids
  the severe random-I/O slowdown on large datasets.

iSAX
----

- Added dynamic, variance-driven root-cardinality splitting for symbolic
  transforms and support for SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words.
- Added full-word node MBR pruning and transform-specific lower bounds,
  including SIMD-capable exact-distance paths where available.
- Improved parallel index construction and hybrid query scheduling, including
  configurable worker/queue counts and robust queue ownership.
- Unified iSAX and trie benchmark summaries, CSV logs, coverage reporting,
  construction timings, and optional per-phase query profiling.

Benchmark runners
-----------------

- `run_dataset.sh` now prints compact K/M/G configuration counts and an
  end-of-run table of query work, coverage, and wall time for all methods run.
- `run_suite.sh` accepts `--index-type isax|trie` to run a regular suite across
  all configured datasets with either layout.
- iSAX runner tight-bound pruning is enabled by default, while variance-driven
  root cardinalities are opt-in with `--dynamic-root-split-variance`; trie
  MBR/split dimensions follow each dataset's coefficient setting and can
  be overridden with `--trie-mbr-dims` (16--128, capped by series length);
  trie fanout is configurable with `--trie-fanout 2|4|8`.
- Trie suite and dataset runners forward the record-MBR suffix and leaf
  k-means options, along with record-prefix, MBR-width, split-width, leaf,
  sampling, queue, NUMA, and input-override settings.  Runner and MESSI logs
  again default to `$HOME/MESSI_logs` (overridable with `MESSI_LOG_ROOT`).

Python API
----------

- Aligned `Index` defaults with the benchmark runners: iSAX tight-bound
  pruning and trie record-MBR suffix pruning are enabled, while variance-based
  iSAX root splitting and trie leaf IVF remain opt-in.
- Added `dynamic_root_split_variance` to the native and Python APIs, with
  validation for iSAX SFA, SPARTAN, and PISA only.  Default SFA coefficient
  pools are capped at 64 dimensions for iSAX and widen automatically to the
  full trie transform width.
- Made the standalone API own its query-reporting default so the Python
  extension no longer depends on the CLI entry point for linking.

Build integration
-----------------

- Kept generated Autotools configuration headers out of source control, so
  local configure/build output does not pollute commits.
- Autotools detects CBLAS headers and `cblas_sgemm`; `build_local.sh` and
  `build_sonic.sh` preserve FFTW, OpenBLAS/LAPACK, CBLAS, and compiler flags
  across configure rechecks.
